    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488">

                <pb facs="0677" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/449: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-29T23:00:00+02:00">March 29, 1934—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 29—7:44 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18. Turkish Government consents definitely to arrest and detain Insull on
                    receiving from me certified copy of complete text of (1) warrant of arrest and
                    (2) judicial record. These must be cabled in full to reach me Friday.<anchor
                        n="40" xml:id="d488-f1"/> Meantime Government will endeavor to detain
                    Insull’s ship until Saturday morning, being powerless to proceed with arrest
                    until documents mentioned are in hand.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
